# Baseline B-21 (F-48): a relationship result encodes as the Bolt 4.4
# Relationship structure 0x52 [id, start node id, end node id, type,
# properties]. "*" is a wildcard only as a map value, not as a structure
# field, so the ids are pinned: they are the ones this script's own fresh
# :memory: server assigns its first relationship and its two nodes.
!: BOLT 4.4
!: AUTO HELLO
!: AUTO GOODBYE

C: RUN "CREATE (a:BoltProbe)-[r:BOLT_PROBE {since: 2020}]->(b:BoltProbe) RETURN r" {} {}
   PULL {"n": -1}
S: SUCCESS {}
   RECORD [{"#52": [0, 0, 1, "BOLT_PROBE", {"since": 2020}]}]
   SUCCESS {}
